{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgHXPtXdbA1Mik6aLnisQy","type":"tool_result","content":"2858\tdef family_context_telemetry(family, data):\n2859\t    \"\"\"Session id + context occupancy/window/percent, read straight off the\n2860\t    process's OWN JSON result (WI-535, telemetry first — no mint, no resume,\n2861\t    no adapter; that's the retention layer, WI-540). Returns\n2862\t    `(session_id, occupancy, window, pct)`, every field `\"\"` where the\n2863\t    family's plain one-shot call doesn't carry it today.\n2864\t\n2865\t    ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already carries `session_id`. Occupancy is\n2866\t    its four usage counters summed (plan §3.3: input + cache_read +\n2867\t    cache_creation + output). Window is the unique `modelUsage` entry whose\n2868\t    same four counters match; absent/ambiguous matches stay blank rather than\n2869\t    guessed (plan §2). This distinguishes the session's own turn from a\n2870\t    colliding subagent aside. Duplicate full matches remain ambiguous even if\n2871\t    their windows agree. OPENAI/OPENCODE's one-shot templates emit none of\n2872\t    this yet; WI-540's per-family adapter is what adds it.\"\"\"\n2873\t    if family != \"ANTHROPIC\":\n2874\t        return \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"\n2875\t    session_id = data.get(\"session_id\") or \"\"\n2876\t    usage = data.get(\"usage\") or {}\n2877\t    usage_fields = (\n2878\t        (\"input_tokens\", \"inputTokens\"),\n2879\t        (\"output_tokens\", \"outputTokens\"),\n2880\t        (\"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"cacheReadInputTokens\"),\n2881\t        (\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cacheCreationInputTokens\"),\n2882\t    )\n2883\t    if not any(usage.get(key) is not None for key, _ in usage_fields):\n2884\t        return session_id, \"\", \"\", \"\"\n2885\t    usage_totals = tuple(usage.get(key) or 0 for key, _ in usage_fields)\n2886\t    occupancy = sum(usage_totals)\n2887\t    matches = [\n2888\t        entry\n2889\t        for entry in (data.get(\"modelUsage\") or {}).values()\n2890\t        if tuple(entry.get(key) or 0 for _, key in usage_fields) == usage_totals\n2891\t    ]\n2892\t    window = \"\"\n2893\t    if len(matches) == 1:\n2894\t        window = matches[0].get(\"contextWindow\", \"\") or \"\"\n2895\t    pct = round(occupancy * 100 / window) if isinstance(window, int) and window else \"\"\n2896\t    return session_id, occupancy, window, pct\n2897\t\n2898\t\n2899\tdef session_meta(\n2900\t    ctx, plan, data, session, stamp, wi_label, outcome, commits, code, wall_secs\n2901\t):\n2902\t    \"\"\"The session log's row, projected from the agent's JSON result. Stays a\n2903\t    dict rather than a record because it IS the log's column set — write_session_log\n2904\t    writes exactly these keys, in this order.\n2905\t\n2906\t    Where the wall time went: API round-trips vs local tool execution (the gap\n2907\t    is the harness running gates/tools). Blank when the CLI reported no JSON\n2908\t    result — the wall clock still stands.\n2909\t\n2910\t    Session-shape telemetry (WI-124): why a session was slow, not just that it\n2911\t    was. ttft = boot-to-first-token (the initial context-ingest latency); cache\n2912\t    read/create = context volume carried per turn / ingested fresh at session\n2913\t    start; effort + fast-mode name the two per-turn speed dials so their\n2914\t    experiments are measurable per row; prompt-chars sizes the instruction the\n2915\t    coordinator composed. All blank when the CLI reported no JSON (the\n2916\t    effort/prompt pair still stands — the coordinator knows what it launched).\n2917\t    \"\"\"\n2918\t    prompt = plan[\"prompt\"]\n2919\t    phase = plan[\"phase\"]\n2920\t    usage = data.get(\"usage\") or {}\n2921\t    session_id, ctx_used, ctx_window, ctx_pct = family_context_telemetry(\n2922\t        plan.get(\"route_family\") or \"\", data"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a03bf2e3-d14c-400d-bc0c-811a86635be0","uuid":"bf7c0169-7fda-45c5-b1cf-7acf3fa2b5ef","timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:12:29.687Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-535-adjudicator-telemetry-first\\project-trajectory\\scripts\\agent_loop.py","content":"def family_context_telemetry(family, data):\n    \"\"\"Session id + context occupancy/window/percent, read straight off the\n    process's OWN JSON result (WI-535, telemetry first — no mint, no resume,\n    no adapter; that's the retention layer, WI-540). Returns\n    `(session_id, occupancy, window, pct)`, every field `\"\"` where the\n    family's plain one-shot call doesn't carry it today.\n\n    ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already carries `session_id`. Occupancy is\n    its four usage counters summed (plan §3.3: input + cache_read +\n    cache_creation + output). Window is the unique `modelUsage` entry whose\n    same four counters match; absent/ambiguous matches stay blank rather than\n    guessed (plan §2). This distinguishes the session's own turn from a\n    colliding subagent aside. Duplicate full matches remain ambiguous even if\n    their windows agree. OPENAI/OPENCODE's one-shot templates emit none of\n    this yet; WI-540's per-family adapter is what adds it.\"\"\"\n    if family != \"ANTHROPIC\":\n        return \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"\n    session_id = data.get(\"session_id\") or \"\"\n    usage = data.get(\"usage\") or {}\n    usage_fields = (\n        (\"input_tokens\", \"inputTokens\"),\n        (\"output_tokens\", \"outputTokens\"),\n        (\"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"cacheReadInputTokens\"),\n        (\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cacheCreationInputTokens\"),\n    )\n    if not any(usage.get(key) is not None for key, _ in usage_fields):\n        return session_id, \"\", \"\", \"\"\n    usage_totals = tuple(usage.get(key) or 0 for key, _ in usage_fields)\n    occupancy = sum(usage_totals)\n    matches = [\n        entry\n        for entry in (data.get(\"modelUsage\") or {}).values()\n        if tuple(entry.get(key) or 0 for _, key in usage_fields) == usage_totals\n    ]\n    window = \"\"\n    if len(matches) == 1:\n        window = matches[0].get(\"contextWindow\", \"\") or \"\"\n    pct = round(occupancy * 100 / window) if isinstance(window, int) and window else \"\"\n    return session_id, occupancy, window, pct\n\n\ndef session_meta(\n    ctx, plan, data, session, stamp, wi_label, outcome, commits, code, wall_secs\n):\n    \"\"\"The session log's row, projected from the agent's JSON result. Stays a\n    dict rather than a record because it IS the log's column set — write_session_log\n    writes exactly these keys, in this order.\n\n    Where the wall time went: API round-trips vs local tool execution (the gap\n    is the harness running gates/tools). Blank when the CLI reported no JSON\n    result — the wall clock still stands.\n\n    Session-shape telemetry (WI-124): why a session was slow, not just that it\n    was. ttft = boot-to-first-token (the initial context-ingest latency); cache\n    read/create = context volume carried per turn / ingested fresh at session\n    start; effort + fast-mode name the two per-turn speed dials so their\n    experiments are measurable per row; prompt-chars sizes the instruction the\n    coordinator composed. All blank when the CLI reported no JSON (the\n    effort/prompt pair still stands — the coordinator knows what it launched).\n    \"\"\"\n    prompt = plan[\"prompt\"]\n    phase = plan[\"phase\"]\n    usage = data.get(\"usage\") or {}\n    session_id, ctx_used, ctx_window, ctx_pct = family_context_telemetry(\n        plan.get(\"route_family\") or \"\", data","numLines":65,"startLine":2858,"totalLines":4101}}}
